# Three.js / Vite gameplay

- Entry: `src/main.ts` (rAF + fixed 60 Hz timestep), game loop in `src/game.ts`
- Rendering setup in `src/render/` (renderer, fog, lights, `EffectComposer` + `UnrealBloomPass`, camera rig)
- Scene content builders under `src/world/` (each returns `{ group, update(t) }`)
- Systems under `src/systems/` (input, particles); UI is a DOM overlay under `src/ui/`
- Merge static geometry (`BufferGeometryUtils.mergeGeometries`) instead of spawning hundreds of meshes
- Point lights use tamed `decay`; a physical inverse-square light next to the camera blows out the frame
- No Phaser, no Unity APIs in this repo; procedural/code-built art only, original IP
- Prefer small focused modules; keep the build playable after every slice
- Mobile-friendly controls when extending input; desktop keyboard + mouse remains primary
